      "reason": "All six source hypotheses and structural binders match sealed Header98; c/Phi differ only by xRef-to-r bound-variable rename, while R/rate/U are identical. The theorem introduces these let definitions with intro; they are not arbitrary map or derivative providers. CompleteSpace is derived internally from FiniteDimensional, with no new public assumption."
    },
    {
      "topic": "actual producer extraction",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "ActualHarmonicFlow supplies actual joint continuity and coordinate ODE ho at every real s. ActualBounceRate supplies actual joint rate continuity hb.2.1. The flow position derivative is sqrt eta times momentum; the momentum derivative is minus reciprocal sqrt eta times x-y minus sqrt eta times grad V(r). These are the literal flow coordinates, not the conserved centered-energy identity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "forward and reverse continuity",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "Fixing y,r,z in the actual jointly continuous Phi gives continuous t->Phi_t z. Pairing with constant r and actual rate continuity gives the forward rate. Pairing flow position with the negated momentum gives R(Phi_t z) continuously, hence the reverse rate. Therefore both rates are interval-integrable for any ordered or reversed real endpoints a,b."
    },
    {
      "topic": "positive-part algebra",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "hdiff unfolds rate and R, uses inner(-p,h)=-inner(p,h), and splits a=inner(p,h) into a>=0 and a<0. In both cases max(0,a)-max(0,-a)=a. It obtains rate(q)-rate(Rq)=sqrt eta inner(p,grad V(x)-grad V(r)) for every phase, including a=0."
    },
    {
      "topic": "target-energy derivative signs and scales",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "The V derivative is derived from ContDiff2 and its actual gradient, composed with hx. HasDerivAt.norm_sq differentiates both x-y and momentum quadratics, including zero vectors. The derivative sum is sqrt eta<grad V(x),p>+(sqrt eta/eta)<x-y,p>-(1/sqrt eta)<p,x-y>-sqrt eta<p,grad V(r)>. Eta>0 gives sqrt eta nonzero and its square=eta, so the middle terms cancel and hdiff identifies the remaining exact rate difference. No incorrect conservation of target U is assumed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "oriented FTC and difference integrals",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "hp.intervalIntegrable and hm.intervalIntegrable supply hi,hj on arbitrary a,b. integral_sub hi hj rewrites the two integrals as the integral of their difference. integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt uses hd on every point in uIcc and hi.sub hj; taking symmetry returns U(Phi_b z)-U(Phi_a z). No time nonnegativity or a<=b assumption is introduced."
    },
    {
      "topic": "degeneracies and scope",
      "result": "PASS",
      "reason": "a=b gives zero energy increment and zero integrals; reversed endpoints use oriented FTC; rank-zero E and zero phase vectors are admitted; zero gradient defect gives zero signed rate difference. Eta=0 remains excluded exactly by the original binder. U may be negative. There is no n, event tuple or Gamma in this fragment, so it proves only the arc producer; bounce U-invariance, finite clamped-path stitching/telescoping and final Gibbs exponent equality still require separate work."
    }
